Angry Grannies is a small Townsville U3A coding collective that creates friendly apps that are fun, accessible and a
little bit different. U3A, the University of the Third Age, is a community learning organisation for mostly seniors,
where members share knowledge, learn new skills and take part in interest-based classes.

Angry Grannies grew out of the U3A Townsville computer programming class, where participants start from scratch, using
Python. They learn how to program by breaking down problems into small, logical and easy steps and then using
those to build the computer code - in many ways like learning a language.

The group’s first app, SuDoKu Playtime, reflects that spirit: it is a colourful, approachable and very different
Sudoku-style game designed for relaxed play, enjoyment and gentle brain training.

We rejoice in being 'ancient'!